---
title: Smashed Cucumber Salad (Pai Huang Gua 拍黄瓜)
description: A refreshing, tangy, and garlicky cold appetizer. Smashing the cucumbers creates jagged edges that soak up the flavorful dressing.
prep time: 10 minutes
cook time: 0 minutes
servings: 2
tags:
  - cucumber
  - vegetable
  - salad
  - cold
  - chinese
  - appetizer
cuisine: Chinese
course: Appetizer
---

> Smashing the cucumber instead of just slicing it is essential for the texture and flavor absorption.

== Prepare Cucumber ==

Wash the @English cucumbers{2%whole}. Place a large #cleaver{} or heavy knife flat on top of the cucumber and firmly smash down until the cucumber splits open.

Cut the smashed cucumber into bite-sized, roughly 1-inch diagonal pieces. Place them in a large #bowl{}.

== Salt the Cucumber ==

Add @salt{½%tsp} to the cucumbers and toss well. Let it sit for ~{10%minutes} to draw out excess moisture. Drain any liquid that pools at the bottom of the bowl.

== Make the Dressing ==

Mince the @garlic{3%cloves}.
In a small #bowl{}, mix the dressing ingredients:
- minced garlic
- @black vinegar{2%tbsp}
- @soy sauce{1%tbsp}
- @sugar{1%tsp}
- @chili oil{1%tbsp} (optional, adjust to taste)
- @toasted sesame oil{1%tsp}

== Toss and Serve ==

Pour the dressing over the drained cucumbers. Toss thoroughly to coat.

Let it marinate in the fridge for ~{10%minutes} before serving for the best flavor. Garnish with @toasted sesame seeds{1%tsp} if desired.